{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790684824,"nonce":"rZbKS+5ERX0a1pAG2SYtMCXZ3jc=","title":"Abstract constructor inlining drops class-to-interface coercion","message":"An abstract backed by an interface can inline `this = source` from its constructor by substituting a concrete class argument directly. The replacement retains the raw class pointer, but abstract methods read the underlying value as an interface fat pointer.\n\nUpstream Issue9770 crashes in A1.get_v on the tiered path. The reduced AbstractInterfaceConstruction fixture fails its first field/method assertion with the existing release binary. The regression also covers a typedef alias, an already-wrapped interface argument, object identity after mutation, and evaluation count.\n\nPreserve the formal interface parameter conversion during constructor substitution, using the existing safe class-to-interface cast lowering. Resolve typedefs before deciding whether the representation conversion is required.","files":null}]}